Hello again,
Had to fix a few things with the DS15:  a suspected failing power supply tu=
rned out to be the front panel power-on button's wires having a flimsy conn=
ection (probably due to front access storage cage removal/installation).  A=
lso had to clone my Debian Alpha installation since the hard drive was shut=
ting down after a while of use -smartctl reported it to be OK, but it also =
reported way too many gigabytes processed during its lifetime.  The machine=
 is now running kernel 5.8.1.

My only line on sources.list is;

deb http://ftp.de.debian.org/debian-ports sid main

I can't install vlc, kodi, cinnamon and several other packages.
Error while trying to install vlc is:

The following information may help to resolve the situation:

The following packages have unmet dependencies:
 vlc-plugin-base : Depends: vlc-data (=3D 3.0.11-3) but 3.0.11.1-1 is to be=
 installed
                   Depends: libavcodec58 (>=3D 7:4.2)
                   Depends: libavformat58 (>=3D 7:4.2) but it is not going =
to be installed
                   Depends: libprotobuf-lite22 (>=3D 3.11.4) but it is not =
installable
                   Depends: libx265-179 (>=3D 3.2) but it is not installabl=
e
 vlc-plugin-video-output : Depends: libavcodec58 (>=3D 7:4.0)


As I posted last month, my old version of iceweasel was deleted by apt.
I downloaded the deb file for firefox 52.6 alpha, but when trying to instal=
l I get the following errors:

Preparing to unpack firefox-esr_52.6.0esr-2+alpha.2_alpha.deb ...
Adding 'diversion of /usr/bin/firefox to /usr/bin/firefox.real by firefox-e=
sr'
Unpacking firefox-esr (52.6.0esr-2+alpha.2) ...
dpkg: dependency problems prevent configuration of firefox-esr:
 firefox-esr depends on libevent-2.1-6 (>=3D 2.1.8-stable); however:
  Package libevent-2.1-6 is not installed.
 firefox-esr depends on libhunspell-1.6-0; however:
  Package libhunspell-1.6-0 is not installed.
 firefox-esr depends on libvpx5 (>=3D 1.6.0); however:
  Package libvpx5 is not installed.

I have newer versions of libhunspell (libhunspell-1.7-0 version 1.7.0-3), l=
ibvpx (libvpx6 version 1.8.2-1) and libevent (libevent-2.1-7 version 2.1.12=
-stable-1).
I can somehow force firefox to install and startup if I link the newer libs=
 with the ones firefox searches for while starting up, but then everytime I=
 try to update with apt I get the reminder that firefox is not properly ins=
talled and can't upgrade anything else.

Is anyone having similar issues?

